bbb-plugin-remote-desktop (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Source package now builds a second binary, bbb-wss-proxy: a
    WebSocket-to-VNC gateway that authenticates incoming connections
    against BBB's session-token API (/bigbluebutton/api/enter). The
    plugin automatically appends the user's session token to every
    share URL, so any user authenticated to a meeting reaches the
    VNC backend with valid credentials and no separate sign-in.
  * Action-bar buttons can now use custom PNG/SVG/JPEG/GIF/WebP
    images or data URIs as icons, in addition to the built-in
    plugin icons and BBB stock icons. URL-shaped values (containing
    "://", leading "/", "data:", or an image-file extension) are
    rendered as a 24x24 <img>.
  * README rewritten for a general (non-collaborate) audience:
    use-case framing, server-side requirements, operator-selector
    documentation, clipboard-sharing documentation, custom-icon
    examples, and an "optional bbb-wss-proxy" install section.
  * Add MIT LICENSE and DEP-5 debian/copyright.

 -- Brent Baccala <cosine@freesoft.org>  Thu, 14 May 2026 04:23:44 +0000

bbb-plugin-remote-desktop (0.2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Skip the force-reconnect on initial content entry to layout. The
    force-reconnect was firing on every fresh page load (not only on
    post-screenshare re-entry), producing two back-to-back websocket
    opens — one from the initial VncDisplay mount, one from the key
    change to 1. That double-connect raced websockify's check-and-spawn
    and, for moderator/teacher sessions, also raced two inetd
    teacher_desktop sessions on the same X display.

 -- Brent Baccala <cosine@freesoft.org>  Wed, 22 Apr 2026 23:30:00 +0000

